              "body_preview": "<!-- function closeWindow() { self.close(); } //--> WebCivil Supreme - Case Detail Court:Queens Supreme Court Index Number:709115/2026 Case Name:In the Matter of the Application of ALBERT BALDEO vs. Addabbo Jr., Joseph P. et al Case Type:SP-Election Law Track:Standard RJI Filed: 03/30/2026 Date NOI Due: 03/30/2027 NOI Filed: Disposition Date: 04/30/2026 Calendar Number: Jury Status: Justice Name: Kerrigan, Hon. Kevin Plaintiff/Petitioner: In the Matter of the Application of ALBERT BALDEO Defendant/Respondent: THE BOARD OF ELECTIONSO F THE CITY OF NEW YORK, For a Judgment pursuant to CPLR Article 78, Election Law Article 16, and CPLR 3001 declaring that Respondent Candidate Joseph P. Addabbo, Jr. has not established and has not maintained a bona fide residence office of New York State Senator for the 15th Senatorial District; declaring that any future designating or nominating petitions filed on his behalf are null and void ab initio; and enjoining the New York City Board of Elections from accepting, processing Addabbo Jr., Joseph P. Attorney/Firm For Plaintiff: MURTAGH, COSSU, VENDITTI & CASTRO-BLANCO, LLP Attorney Type: RETAINED Atty. Status: Active 222 BLOOMINGDALE RD WHITE PLAIN",
